00:09:39,848 --> 00:09:42,062
2 lines of code which we required before,

228
00:09:42,335 --> 00:09:44,870
which we had to read, and we just got 1 line

229
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:48,400
of code which is 100% clear about what it

230
00:09:48,432 --> 00:09:48,625
does.

231
00:09:49,331 --> 00:09:51,674
That's the Law of Dameter and how you should

232
00:09:51,722 --> 00:09:54,257
follow it, and that's why it matters for

233
00:09:54,369 --> 00:09:55,797
writing clean code.

234
00:09:56,937 --> 00:10:00,643
And as a side note, and why I also wanted to

235
00:10:00,643 --> 00:10:02,617
include this in the course, which is of

236
00:10:02,649 --> 00:10:03,547
course not

237
00:10:04,077 --> 00:10:06,403
just about object-oriented programming and

